/**
 * A screen showing the sheet as of a date (?asOf=yyyy-MM-dd on its reads): each read of the sheet runs in a
 * transaction that first puts the sheet as it stood at the end of that date (see {@link SheetSnapshots#show}) and is
 * always rolled back, so every figure the endpoints make is made from that state, with the date for the sheet's
 * today, and nothing is ever written. Every change sent while the as-of date is set is refused (see ViewerGuard).
/**
 * Every row a sheet holds, kept as its today moves on (sheet_snapshot), so the sheet can be shown as it stood at the
 * end of a date. The tables kept are found on boot: every table with a sheet column (the sheet table by its id) and
 * every table of rows kept per person (a person_id column); each gets a shadow table {@code <table>__ASOF} with the
 * same columns (bar the generated ones) and a snapshot_id. A table added later is kept with no change here.
    /** Tables that are history themselves, never part of what a sheet shows. */
    /** A table kept per sheet: its stored columns and how its rows of one sheet are found. */
    /** In the order a parent comes before the rows that reference it. */
    /** Finds the tables kept per sheet and makes their shadow tables (DDL, so once on boot, outside any change). */
    /** Keeps every row the sheet holds now, as its today moves from one date to another. */
    /**
     * Puts the sheet, inside the caller's transaction, as it stood at the end of the date: the rows kept when its today
     * first moved from on or before the date to after it; what it holds now when its today has never moved past the
     * date; nothing when its today was never on or before it. The date then stands in for its today. The caller must
     * roll back.
/**
 * What a sheet holds at one moment that its figures are made from: its people, claims (with their status logs) and
 * rates, the recorded values of its floor, late percent and cap, and its policy date ("" when none is set), and each grade's recorded grace (null in a state kept before graces). Read
 * {@link #on} a date, it stands as it would with that date for the sheet's today.
    /** The person with the id as they stand with the date for the sheet's today; null when they were not on the sheet. */
    /** The person's claims as they stand with the date for the sheet's today, newest first. */
    /** The floor by date. */
    /** What makes the late charges with the date for the sheet's today. */
    /** The cap in force on the date, or null when there is none. */
/**
 * The sheet as it stood at the end of each of its todays: when the sheet's today moves on, what it holds is kept,
 * so a date's state is the one kept when the today first moved from on or before that date to after it.
    /** What the sheet holds now. */
    /** Keeps what the sheet holds now, as its today moves from one date to another. */
    /**
     * What the sheet held at the end of the date, before its today: the state kept when the today first moved from on
     * or before it to after it; null when the today was never on or before it.
/**
 * Terms count business days: every claim kept takes as its due-by the terms-th business day after its date, skipping
 * Saturdays, Sundays and the sheet's holidays as they stand now. The terms are those it was fixed with: its person's
 * own, else those of the person's grade on its date, else the sheet's on its date (14 when none is set).
/**
 * A claim keeps the terms its due-by was fixed with, so adding a holiday can work its due-by out again. Every claim kept
 * takes the terms it would be fixed with now: its person's own, else those of the person's grade on its date, else the
 * sheet's on its date (14 when none is set).
package net.officefloor.hq.app.sheet;


public class SaveToday {
    public void save(@PathVariable("sheet") String sheet, @RequestParam("user") String user, @Val LocalDate today,
            SheetClock clock, PeriodCloser closer, Rollup rollup, Claims claims, SheetStates states, SheetSnapshots snapshots,
            Audit audit) {
        Rollup.Snapshot before = rollup.take(sheet);
        // A change of today releases every claim editor's lock on the sheet.
        LocalDate was = clock.today(sheet);
        if (!today.equals(was)) {
            // Each person's due-total as it stood on the day being left, in list order.
            for (Rollup.Figures figures : before.people().values()) {
                audit.record("SNAPSHOT sheet=" + sheet + " by=" + user + " name=" + figures.name() + " due-total="
                        + figures.dueTotal());
            }
            claims.unlockAll(sheet);
            // What the sheet holds at the end of its old today is kept, for a statement taken as of that date.
            states.keep(sheet, was, today);
            // Every row it holds is kept too, for the screen shown as of that date.
            snapshots.keep(sheet, was, today);
        }
        clock.setToday(sheet, today);
        // Periods past their grace days close before the figures the today change moved are audited.
        closer.autoClose(sheet, user);
        rollup.record(sheet, user, before);
    }
}

